---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Lunixia Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Lunixia wellness, journaling, health, mood tracking, and spirituality app."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Lunixia Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: June 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia is a personal wellness, self-reflection, mood tracking,
          journaling, health, productivity, and spirituality application
          designed to help users better understand themselves and build healthy
          daily habits.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information Lunixia stores, how it
          is used, and how you remain in control of your information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data You Create</h2>
        <p>
          Information created within Lunixia may include mood logs, journal
          entries, health records, medication schedules, symptom logs, notes,
          reminders, exercise records, self-care activities, points, goals,
          reflections, and user preferences.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is stored locally on your device and may synchronize
          through your personal iCloud account if CloudKit synchronization is
          enabled.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>iCloud & CloudKit</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may use Apple's CloudKit framework to synchronize information
          between your Apple devices through your personal iCloud account.
        </p>

        <p>
          The developer of Lunixia does not have access to your private CloudKit
          database.
        </p>

        <p>
          Apple's handling of iCloud data is governed by Apple's privacy policy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Mood Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may store mood check-ins, emotional reflections, activities,
          mood tags, mood history, and related wellness information entered by
          the user.
        </p>

        <p>
          Mood information is used solely to provide mood tracking, trend
          analysis, insights, and personal reflection features within the app.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Mood Statistics & Insights</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may generate statistics, charts, summaries, trends, and
          insights based on mood information you choose to record.
        </p>

        <p>
          These calculations are generated solely to provide personal wellness
          insights and are not used for advertising or profiling purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Phone Usage Statistics</h2>
        <p>
          If permission is granted, Lunixia may access screen time information,
          device activity data, and app usage statistics through Apple's
          approved APIs.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is used exclusively to provide wellness insights,
          digital wellbeing features, and usage reports within the app.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Journaling</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may store journal entries, journal books, tags, prompts,
          reflections, notes, and other content created by the user.
        </p>

        <p>
          Journal content remains private and is not shared with advertisers or
          third parties.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>AI Journal Features</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may provide optional AI-powered features such as journal
          prompt generation, journal analysis, writing assistance, summaries,
          and reflection tools.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information submitted to these features may be processed by approved
          AI service providers solely for the purpose of generating the
          requested results.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Health Information</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may store health-related information entered by the user,
          including vital signs, exercise records, medication schedules,
          medication history, symptom logs, water intake, step counts, and
          wellness tracking information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Health information is used exclusively to provide the health and
          wellness features of the app.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Apple Health Integration</h2>
        <p>
          If enabled by the user, Lunixia may read information from or write
          information to Apple Health through HealthKit.
        </p>

        <p>
          HealthKit information is governed by Apple's HealthKit policies and
          remains under the user's control.
        </p>

        <p>
          HealthKit data is never used for advertising, marketing, or data
          broker purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Medication Management</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may store medication names, schedules, dosage information,
          refill reminders, completion history, and medication-related notes.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information exists solely to support medication management and
          reminder functionality.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Sticky Notes</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia includes note-taking and sticky note features that allow users
          to store reminders, thoughts, plans, and personal information for
          their own use.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Self-Care Points & Achievements</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia includes optional points, achievements, rewards, streaks, and
          progress systems designed to encourage consistency and self-care.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information remains private to your account and is not used for
          advertising or profiling purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Spiritual Features</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may provide spiritual and reflective tools including lunar
          phase information, daily tarot cards, daily Lenormand cards,
          horoscopes, and related content.
        </p>

        <p>
          These features are intended for personal reflection and entertainment
          purposes only.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia uses local notifications to deliver reminders related to
          journaling, medications, health tracking, self-care activities,
          habits, and other app features.
        </p>

        <p>Notification scheduling occurs directly on your device.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Widgets</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may provide Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets displaying
          mood information, health progress, reminders, self-care activities,
          points, and wellness insights.
        </p>

        <p>
          Widget information is shared locally between the app and widget
          extensions using Apple's App Group system.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia does not sell personal information and does not use
          third-party advertising networks or behavioral advertising systems.
        </p>

        <p>
          Lunixia does not share personal wellness, journaling, health, or mood
          information with advertisers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia may offer optional premium features or subscriptions through
          Apple's StoreKit framework.
        </p>

        <p>
          Payment processing is handled entirely by Apple. Lunixia does not
          collect, store, or have access to payment information, billing
          information, or credit card numbers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Lunixia is not directed toward children under the age of 13 and does
          not knowingly collect personal information from children.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You maintain control over your information at all times. Mood logs,
          journal entries, health records, medication information, notes,
          reflections, and other content may be deleted directly within the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting the app removes locally stored data from your device. If
          CloudKit synchronization is enabled, synced information may also be
          managed through your Apple ID and iCloud settings.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new
          features, legal requirements, platform changes, or improvements to the
          app. Updated versions will be published on this page with a revised
          effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or how Lunixia handles
          your information, you can contact:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
